  = note: operands are never converted implicitly, inside an `#[algebraic]` scope or outside one
  = note: if these are numeric types, cast one of them; if `T` is not opted in yet, add `reassoc::passthrough!(T);`, or wrap the expression in `strict!(..)` to use ordinary operators
  = note: if `T` is a generic type parameter, none of those apply: dispatch is resolved per concrete type, so `#[algebraic]` cannot be used in a generic function
  = help: the following other types implement trait `MulRhs<Lhs, O, Tag>`:
            `&Duration` implements `MulRhs<&u32, Duration>`
            `&Duration` implements `MulRhs<u32, Duration>`
